{"title":"2019 AIME I Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Fake_Solve)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Fake Solve)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Newton&#39;s_Sums)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Newton's Sums)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Official_MAA_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Official MAA 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Official_MAA_2)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Official MAA 2)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by The Power of Logic</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_&amp;_More_by_MegaMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution &amp; More by MegaMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For distinct complex numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecdf0b75892329cca4a4a85a7412a22282e5a035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1,z_2,\\dots,z_{673}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"108\" height=\"11\" />, the polynomial\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/b/35b2995ac0fe946045c887ed51b6c5a4920ade87.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x-z_1)^3(x-z_2)^3 \\cdots (x-z_{673})^3\\]\" width=\"248\" height=\"19\" />can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f5255f37eb4650a56b9997e5b6e65d535cb1c0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2019} + 20x^{2018} + 19x^{2017}+g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"248\" height=\"19\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is a polynomial with complex coefficients and with degree at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b781fdf1cd172b567be38e2ffa6f20f0b8390c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />. The sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/4/8f41f0be45a01d496350a366e307c73e63020126.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left| \\sum_{1 \\le j &lt;k \\le 673} z_jz_k \\right|\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"55\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In order to begin this problem, we must first understand what it is asking for. The notation \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/4/8f41f0be45a01d496350a366e307c73e63020126.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left| \\sum_{1 \\le j &lt;k \\le 673} z_jz_k \\right|\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"55\" />\nsimply asks for the absolute value of the sum of the product of the distinct unique roots of the polynomial taken two at a time or\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/6/0263dcdfd19a3abff591649aafb8e681f852cc81.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(z_1z_2+z_1z_3+ \\dots + z_1z_{672}+z_1z_{673})+(z_2z_3+z_2z_4+ \\dots +z_2z_{673}) + (z_3z_4+z_3z_5+ \\dots +z_3z_{673}) + \\dots +z_{672}z_{673}.\\]\" width=\"756\" height=\"18\" /> Call this sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Now we can begin the problem. Rewrite the polynomial as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/5/5c5cb0f34d8790e60f476df1289662c162f67cf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=(x-z_1)(x-z_1)(x-z_1)(x-z_2)(x-z_2)(x-z_2) \\dots (x-z_{673})(x-z_{673})(x-z_{673})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"668\" height=\"18\" />. Then we have that the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/6/0567c46b589ec0e004716fe156ab1ecf5c3d09d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1,z_1,z_1,z_2,z_2,z_2, \\dots , z_{673},z_{673},z_{673}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"278\" height=\"11\" />. \n</p><p>By Vieta's formulas, we have that the sum of the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/c/f8c435971393302a63ac0456c7d2c55f7fa94f21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1)^1 \\cdot \\dfrac{20}{1}=-20=z_1+z_1+z_1+z_2+z_2+z_2+ \\dots + z_{673}+z_{673}+z_{673}=3(z_1+z_2+z_3+ \\dots +z_{673})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"798\" height=\"38\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/2/662265cfb673899af435382308adc06306f948f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1+z_2+z_3+ \\dots +z_{673}=- \\dfrac{20}{3}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"251\" height=\"37\" /> \n</p><p>Similarly, we also have that the the sum of the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> taken two at a time is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6827b139ca524becd5e908c9ec1258216af3566.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1)^2 \\cdot \\dfrac{19}{1} = 19.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"126\" height=\"38\" /> This is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba53bb8a6015c91f80a176c92e6023224f89474d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1^2+z_1^2+z_1^2+z_1z_2+z_1z_2+z_1z_2+ \\dots =  \\\\ 3(z_1^2+z_2^2+ \\dots + z_{673}^2) + 9(z_1z_2+z_1z_3+z_1z_4+ \\dots + z_{672}z_{673}) =  3(z_1^2+z_2^2+ \\dots + z_{673}^2) + 9S.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"727\" height=\"39\" /> \n</p><p>Now we need to find and expression for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bd949524112b00240054935396f95de5db02696.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1^2+z_2^2+ \\dots + z_{673}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"19\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. We note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/4/8c483f36471302c78c770c0b460102937d575c1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(z_1+z_2+z_3+ \\dots +z_{673})^2= (-20/3)^2=\\dfrac{400}{9} \\\\ =(z_1^2+z_2^2+ \\dots + z_{673}^2)+2(z_1z_2+z_1z_3+z_1z_4+ \\dots + z_{672}z_{673})=(z_1^2+z_2^2+ \\dots + z_{673}^2)+2S.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"728\" height=\"58\" /> \nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/a/26a7db7f4087be70f030703b103fa88105a674fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1^2+z_2^2+ \\dots + z_{673}^2= \\dfrac{400}{9} -2S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"249\" height=\"37\" />. \n</p><p>Plugging this into our other Vieta equation, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/1/1e16dcef525876eba8d18ae336f355df5ac376b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\left( \\dfrac{400}{9} -2S \\right) +9S = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"198\" height=\"43\" />. This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a724a5f0fb8bf087258180b1dccf40218dcad3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = - \\dfrac{343}{9} \\Rightarrow \\left| S \\right| = \\dfrac{343}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" />. Since 343 is relatively prime to 9, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/929585d4f217d0f8cea9bb0b9af0aac23e3d11f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n = 343+9 = \\fbox{352}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"192\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Fake_Solve.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Fake_Solve)\">Solution 2 (Fake Solve)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Fake Solve)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This is a quick fake solve using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/f/e0f9fdb66c9cd13382e73ced8add205081b5cd30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_i = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/3/9e33307b4552744fb7038877d9c38bca29230413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\le i \\le 673$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"15\" /> and only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/710b0cac14e043476dc15fb96fe839275b75e9a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1,z_2 \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"17\" /> .\n</p><p>By Vieta's, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/9/86924363bd9f0e5d1f59220920a582191764945f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3z_1+3z_2=-20\\]\" width=\"127\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/6/9368454d7a7dcab8c47f9c7dce067182de8912c7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3z_1^2+3z_2^2+9z_1z_2 = 19.\\]\" width=\"182\" height=\"19\" />\nRearranging gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/39563884cfac2f04d63e1436939841c8762116f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1 + z_2 = \\dfrac{-20}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"113\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/4/5c4e073f269fbd7d9efca0fb70f6a922e4ecd912.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(z_1^2 + 2z_1z_2 + z_2^2) + 3z_1z_2 = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"247\" height=\"19\" /> giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e575da50ec1ab26f16d19235ead3b26fcc9ae0a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(z_1 + z_2)^2 + 3z_1z_2 = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"189\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Substituting gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1ac3f79fda19e3fd6aa8aabf7dff9ef8bf78c533.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\left(\\dfrac{400}{9}\\right) + 3z_1z_2 = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"174\" height=\"43\" /> which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/d/b9d401cc3d80ce60fc757111eb1bfb12ddd1edf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{400}{3} + 3z_1z_2 = \\dfrac{57}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"139\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/d/5bd283d398bff14770e230b675c87af3d5be1d93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3z_1z_2 = \\dfrac{-343}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"108\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/9/599f4a2e42cbf78f4aa1079e430e5c559ed2cac8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1z_2 = \\dfrac{-343}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"99\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/0/ac04d3c0c2af3f0ad9c4f3395b02b160a78db66d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\dfrac{-343}{9}|=\\dfrac{343}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"113\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/6/946e2bf671a22341da94e35d32bce7354e3f1ccb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[m+n = 343+9 = \\boxed{352}.\\]\" width=\"198\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/4/7e471b56f5a5f5049eebcc16ec8aafc284f91e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\sum_{1\\le j&lt;k\\le 673} z_jz_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"139\" height=\"40\" />. By Vieta's, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/6/fb6bacb13f883bd60251f72465a72c57535440fd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3\\sum_{i=1}^{673}z_i=-20\\implies \\sum_{i=1}^{673}z_i=-\\frac{20}3.\\]\" width=\"267\" height=\"50\" />Then, consider the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/d/26d0be539a01e5e37d7babc12f221b287537ccc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19x^{2017}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" /> term. To produce the product of two roots, the two roots can either be either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/e/67e997768c70702006bf2a2ed0639f4c6e46b4ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(z_i,z_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f38be33544517dc624552224b87a6fefaf8a1de6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(z_j,z_k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/8/8f8e96ed92da64249f9b7d78bb5b5b46c3073f46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j&lt;k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />. In the former case, this can happen in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/4/584a2d768f8663291f0fb6cd3362cb0d9f81f5d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tbinom 32=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"55\" height=\"22\" /> ways, and in the latter case, this can happen in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee19f2230cc721282aa8253c8d9b7e5ff8ffbe9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2=9$\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" /> ways. Hence,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/2/b123eb1e45874d8f4b13736ff4101aed4a4cad78.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 19=3\\sum_{i=1}^{673} z_i^2+9\\sum_{1\\le j&lt;k\\le 673} z_jz_k=3\\left(\\left(-\\frac{20}3\\right)^2-2x\\right)+9x&amp;=\\frac{400}3+3x\\\\ \\implies x&amp;=-\\frac{343}9, \\end{align*}\" width=\"553\" height=\"99\" />\nand the requested sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/3/7d34541da1536e1add01ec866d63257bc8760ceb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$343+9=\\boxed{352}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/6197191ed5acb0f04404460d49f3563b1c747f1b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(f(x))^3=x^{2019}+20x^{2018}+19x^{2017}+g(x).\\]\" width=\"333\" height=\"19\" /> Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/2/892419e27e4db990a24321d75e742455261441ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=(x-z_{1})(x-z_{1})\\cdots (x-z_{673})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"286\" height=\"18\" />. This is also equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/b/91b437aea4dba3dd4991ac81470c39e1f64d0358.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x)=x^{673}+ax^{672}+bx^{671}+h(x)\\]\" width=\"270\" height=\"19\" /> for some real coefficients <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and some polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/7/1f745cf4286f88b236750e1e9a8abe3dacd9dc39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> with degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a4cf3ebb294df5e93003bf9de36ea15cab3b818.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$670$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. We can see that the big summation expression is simply summing the product of the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> taken two at a time. By Vieta's, this is just the coefficient <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. The first three terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/9/6294c0a595fd626823d609f20a44f87505e814b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(f(x))^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"19\" /> can be bashed in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> to get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/e/4bec5628faeb7c6cb9f59fb1aac67450ce26f1ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[20 = 3a\\]\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/4/b047450df70cb94fdeaf2d7905d1e7e96ef77801.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[19 = 3a^2+3b\\]\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/6/c66f7747d3d0996ae1e91c5147234f683334499e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{20}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"54\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/2/f42f8305a0f7cd01dfd41e05c110e614a4585d45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=\\frac{1}{3}\\left(19-3\\left(\\frac{20}{3} \\right)^2 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"180\" height=\"53\" />. That is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/7/8a7d26b08b371eeaa62665949e832206cea605b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|b|=\\frac{343}{9}=\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"115\" height=\"37\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/a/b6ae4eaf7d50f9ed2e8bb2f630549ca0411bbb78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n=343+9=\\boxed{352}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"195\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Newton.27s_Sums.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Newton's_Sums)\">Solution 5 (Newton's Sums)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Newton&#39;s Sums)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The polynomial has 673 unique roots of multiplicity 3 each, for a total of 2019 roots.\n</p><p>To start, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/1/fe1647d64a42ac3127e0c0d6a86654f11017457b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left| \\sum_{1 \\le j &lt;k \\le 673} z_jz_k \\right|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"115\" height=\"54\" />. Next, let the sum of the roots of the polynomial be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, which is equivalent to the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/3/2c303b8cb6afa106a1f230bc241712fea0a7fb23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(z_1+z_2+\\cdots+z_{673})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"174\" height=\"20\" />, and the sum of squares of these roots be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107c7c8e5a64d81ed24331e510b777b7d08345b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e46ce8367a41a8e6c41838bd7789b80718beba4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(z_1^2+z_2^2+z_3^2+\\dots+z_{673}^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"214\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>By Vieta's,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a10e799b8550a830ee5a8fdbfc38b05dc545090.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3( z_1 + z_2 + z_3 + z_4 \\dots + z_{673}) = -20\\]\" width=\"284\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/f/51f4fab97024750543b442e12bb9223b918b9df2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3( z_1^2 + z_2^2 + z_3^2 + \\dots + z_{673}^2) + 9S = 19\\]\" width=\"297\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a17df6a45ea3ba6e2022caaf0333621f72151ec3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1 = -20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />. Using the definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107c7c8e5a64d81ed24331e510b777b7d08345b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> provided above, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Newton%27s_Sums\" title=\"Newton&#39;s Sums\"> Newton Sums</a> tells us that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cd368ce4e87d4a7f4483641d5ba454587c2c42f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2 + -20 \\cdot P_1 \\cdot + 19 \\cdot 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"175\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/d/e1dddd9e0373e05864ea390f299f542278342983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2 = 362$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"17\" />. Plugging back into the second Vieta's equation yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/9/2c9d0177da5d044ced93afeea7a5584ee5231ed5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[362 + 9S = 19 \\implies S = -\\frac{343}{9}\\]\" width=\"242\" height=\"37\" />\nTaking the absolute value, our answer is therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d03cab99cbe643c36dcd528a492346e1c4af359c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$343 + 9 = \\boxed{352}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"123\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p><br />\nNote: The tripled roots might seem confusing, but it's easily verified that our Vieta's system of equations is correct using combinatorics to find out how many terms we should have. The right hand side of the first equation has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/4/8e48df2420712f464ca443538feeac486b99e113.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\cdot673 = 2019$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"14\" /> terms (exactly what we expect). Unsimplified, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107c7c8e5a64d81ed24331e510b777b7d08345b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> also has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f49e1f42131f302f2b4a45393cdc3fed5be2655c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2019$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> terms and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/2/252ef4686403fdb307d74dd6a9c706ae7b2af774.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{673}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"57\" height=\"55\" /> terms. We want a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/3/153acb3957bcf62cec56bf503b96102ba8948b01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{2019}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"60\" height=\"53\" /> terms, which happens to be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/f/d7f937d3afa429b53885408e93edff35212b9acb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2019 + 9\\cdot\\binom{673}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"138\" height=\"55\" /> so this is correct. \n</p><p>~YBSuburbanTea\n</p><p>~edits by BakedPotato66, faliure167\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Official_MAA_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Official_MAA_1)\">Solution 6 (Official MAA 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Official MAA 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because each root of the polynomial appears with multiplicity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f885f96d2fb7e65f800de4ff71d7dcd0a5d2db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> Viète's Formulas show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/e/1de33c4d7d712b19a2630121a41cba3c9b577c74.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z_1+z_2+\\cdots+z_{673}=-\\frac{20}3\\]\" width=\"207\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/d/cad23869e7d43a2bf48b6d19a70fd52fbb1c81db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z_1^2+z_2^2+\\cdots+z_{673}^2 =\\frac13\\left((-20)^2-2\\cdot19\\right)=\\frac{362}3.\\]\" width=\"382\" height=\"37\" /> Then the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/8/d387efc1b001567ac79730f23fc1a4a5ce9cd38d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{673}z_i\\right)^2=\\sum_{i=1}^{673}z_i^2+2\\left(\\sum_{1\\le j&lt;k\\le 673}z_jz_k\\right)\\]\" width=\"308\" height=\"58\" /> shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/3/2f395834c4c9ef3ca409cba78fed108af5433c28.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{1\\le j&lt;k\\le 673}z_jz_k=\\frac{\\left(-\\frac{20}3\\right)^2-\\frac{362}3}{2}=-\\frac{343}9.\\]\" width=\"307\" height=\"55\" /> The requested sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/6/46682a69600a796721fc5c73f1b1f148d63a7288.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$343+9=352.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Note that such a polynomial does exist. For example, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/5/0d5a9cb8d74411acab351ffef53438e8f37bc40d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{673}=-\\tfrac{20}3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"88\" height=\"21\" /> and for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df6670308b09813288d7171adae7c207f97b25d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1,2,3,\\dots,336,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"145\" height=\"16\" /> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/6/95613538bf58e745fbfaade7e306fee9af7d7696.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z_i=\\sqrt{\\frac{343i}{9\\sum_{j=1}^{336}j}}\\qquad \\text{and}\\qquad z_{i+336}=-z_i.\\]\" width=\"319\" height=\"53\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/737b86bad33deb155a9c7b1346fb6a32828849ac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^{673}z_i=-\\frac{20}3\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\\sum_{i=1}^{673}z_i^2=2\\sum_{i=1}^{336}\\frac{343i}{9\\sum_{i=1}^{336}j}+\\left(\\frac{20}3\\right)^2=\\frac{362}3,\\]\" width=\"507\" height=\"50\" /> as required.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Official_MAA_2.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Official_MAA_2)\">Solution 7 (Official MAA 2)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Official MAA 2)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are constants <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84ef496b64af03ccc9364968da50d0814ca02b1d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x-z_1)(x-z_2)(x-z_3)\\cdots(x-z_{673})=x^{673}+ax^{672}+bx^{671}+\\cdots.\\]\" width=\"522\" height=\"20\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/9/649fae7e1185acdf0a6d2e2b012766b883245e11.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x^{673}+ax^{672}+bx^{671}+\\cdots)^3=x^{2019}+20x^{2018}+19x^{2017}+\\cdots.\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"19\" /> Comparing the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/a/f8a83b1635cc4c47b57a3566479e840813a06af4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2018}$\" width=\"36\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/5/2a5909622c452d2363358ce9073baefc6f263283.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2017}$\" width=\"36\" height=\"15\" /> coefficients shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb1139881de798d0a38ce05b1d9de5be94780775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a=20$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/5/94565a03adfadc7592e4078f6c767e7411813072.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a^2+3b=19.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" /> Solving this system yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/3/dd3288b6179e0e396468670662e86c28bdd3349d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\tfrac{20}3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"49\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/8/8680b1adcb3f21fe5ba3705455be037a859da6ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=-\\tfrac{343}9.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"73\" height=\"21\" /> Viète's Formulas then give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/1/e719eace1823eb6701a718e11b68c11b80d08102.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left|\\sum_{1\\le j&lt;k\\le 673}z_jz_k\\right|=|b|=\\tfrac{343}9,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"212\" height=\"54\" /> as above.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8\">Solution 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that we are trying to find the sum of the products of the pairwise distinct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f756c0f47c2c000ff11cc29f13381232ff401aeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />. First, disregard the repeated roots and call the roots of the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/e/0ae26068fa27430fd8037ddac7dafd2d586afc2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2\\ldots x_{2019}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"13\" /> for simplicity's sake. \n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2c3e7d42555b56df9d6b9eab885f349bdeef25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(z_1+z_2\\ldots z_{2019})^2=2\\sum_{1\\leq j&lt;k\\leq2019}{z_jz_k}+\\sum_{1\\leq k\\leq 2019}{z_k^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -26px\" width=\"393\" height=\"46\" />. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/3/8934dbaebddc6eba21e16d1d3c50cdb6800b381c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{1\\leq j&lt;k\\leq2019} {z_jz_k}=19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -26px\" width=\"157\" height=\"46\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/a/5aa54feffa74b8e524b945ee8b89b8fc7134dbd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1+ x_2\\ldots +x_{2019})^2=20^2=400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"267\" height=\"21\" /> by Vietas so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/2/172592a9d0bbc938d77b9c4fad5c8f86aa22f3dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{1\\leq k\\leq 2019}{z_k^2}=362$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"134\" height=\"45\" />. Also, since every root is repeated 3 times, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/a/baa306e7564f6bd0c77c23ee76114579fce3ac35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{1\\leq k\\leq 2019}{z_k^2}=3\\sum_{1\\leq k\\leq673}{z_k^2} \\Longrightarrow \\sum_{1\\leq k\\leq673}{z_k^2}=\\frac{362}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"363\" height=\"50\" /> where the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f756c0f47c2c000ff11cc29f13381232ff401aeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> in the second sum are all distinct.\n</p><p>Call <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/b/47b2780b34e0078f3cbd1f26004df6b108cd08c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\sum_{1 \\le j &lt;k \\le 673} z_jz_k|=|s|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -26px\" width=\"164\" height=\"46\" />. Taking into account repeated roots, if we pair any two roots together, there will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/3/333b7ef194e85f3865a3c69ec98bc0de7255d77d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{3}{1}=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"70\" height=\"53\" /> copies for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/5/9c5ddac7e82806f2c4252ba9bf4e41fceab0ad52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_k^2, 1\\leq z\\leq 673$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/4/57479e2729ec45042b4ed5e73d9974b88d288922.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\cdot 3=9$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> copies for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/4/234d30cc62ced72087b6b4fec7f6c3aef374be82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_jz_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/2/762a43137e1d61e8a958446459e86ac7ed0022d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f756c0f47c2c000ff11cc29f13381232ff401aeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> are distinct.\n</p><p>Since the sum of any two pairs of roots is 19, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99d63cb2ea7a6a8c1bfe617259b7d6e1cf657f8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9s+3\\sum_{1\\leq k\\leq673}{z_k^2}=19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"171\" height=\"45\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/a/f8ab1132dccff2f6aef620f2b59d8dc94599f524.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9s+362=19 \\Longrightarrow s=\\frac{-343}{9}, |s|=\\frac{343}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"311\" height=\"38\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/066aa6c21d987c4210fee88d3fcdae7d962d1663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n=343+9=352$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"185\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Magnetoninja\">Magnetoninja</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Dp-pw6NNKRo?t=776\">https://youtu.be/Dp-pw6NNKRo?t=776</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic\">Video Solution by The Power of Logic</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by The Power of Logic\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7SFKuEdgwMA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7SFKuEdgwMA</a>\n</p><p>~The Power of Logic\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.26_More_by_MegaMath\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_&amp;_More_by_MegaMath\">Video Solution &amp; More by MegaMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution &amp; More by MegaMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Video #2 (Vieta's Formulas):\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6-kcdBsmCmc\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6-kcdBsmCmc</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I\" title=\"2019 AIME I\">2019 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2019 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2019 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2019\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2019 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2019 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2019 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2019 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2019 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2019 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2019 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2019 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2019 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2019 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2019 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2019 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2019 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2019 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2019 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align: